WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.399
his video is part of Project Homecoming, more
on that later.

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:08.350
The Austro-Hungarian Empire, as its name suggests,
was divided into two parts, the Austrian,

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.480
and the Hungarian.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.049
These parts where then further subdivided,
on the Austrian side today’s Czechia was

00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:18.110
divided in to Bohemia, Moravia and Silesia
and on the Hungarian side today’s Slovakia

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.710
was, ehh just Hungary.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:24.350
Hungary was very particular in it’s idea
of “who cares it’s all mine”.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.030
Then again that’s the idea followed by any
imperial nation not just Hungary.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.260
But I digress.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.450
This direct control of Slovakia by hungary
for about a thousand years but more prominent

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:38.550
in the last 200, meant that Slovaks even though
having a very small number of intelectual

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:43.510
which ended up leading the nationalistic movement
in the 19th and early 20th century, had practically

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.940
speaking no middle or higher class.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.740
Most slovaks where farmers, minors and low
skilled factory workers.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:50.740
And even though there where certain aristocrats
and intellectuals with slovak roots, they

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:51.740
mostly considered themselves as Hungairians
either for practical reasons or actual self

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:52.740
identity.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.740
When we compare that to the Czechs, it’s
a very different picture.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:57.950
Bohemia was a very prominent kingdom within
the HRE and even though it then fell under

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:01.850
the Habsburg control it always retain a certain
kind of autonomy.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:07.150
Meaning the Czech people had a thriving middle
class, an aristocracy and numerous intellectuals.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:11.400
This is not to mean they weren’t restrain
at all by Austrian rules and in fact almost

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.700
any middle or high class Czech had to know
German if they wanted to progress their career

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.510
in any meaningful way.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:22.110
But when compared to the Slovaks they where
leaps ahead in social progress and personal

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.110
freedoms.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:27.430
With all that said by the end of the 19th
century both Czechs and Slovaks were fighting

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:32.510
for some sort of autonomy, whether that be
recognized equality within the Empire or complete

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:35.310
succession from it, depends on who you ask.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:39.630
There where many movements each with a different
goal and a different plan to get there.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:44.280
In Czechia the most prominent political views
by the end of the 19th century didn’t really

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.600
consider Slovakia.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.430
This is not to say there weren’t any Czech
movements for the formation of Czechoslovakia

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:53.740
or at the very least support for the “Slovak
Brothers” in one way or another but none

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:58.370
of these movements by the end of the 19th
century were prevalent in the Czech mindset,

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:03.650
being vastly overshadowed by the Czech fear
of Germanification, which spurred up the Czech

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:07.250
nationalistc movement campaigning for equal
rights and self autonomy.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:11.250
Because if Czechs had the means to administer
their own lands they would no longer have

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.989
to fear and could even counteract Germanification.

00:02:14.989 --> 00:02:20.200
But even though this idea was almost universal
amongst all Czech political parties they disagreed

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.810
on how to tackle it.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:27.390
Nonetheless by far the most prominent movement
was best described by Karel Kramář a Czech

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:33.780
politician, “The lands of the Bohemian crown,
formed an undivided and indivisible whole,

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:39.560
completely independent and autonomous vis-a-vis
the other lands of their King“ hence advocating

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:43.720
for remaining within the Empire while gaining
the autonomy like Hungary had.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.970
And in fact by the end of the 19th century
many Czechs didn’t want to succeed from

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.600
the Empire, they just wanted more autonomy.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:55.350
Swithcing from the Czechs to Slovaks now,
the most prominent and infact the only faction

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:59.450
to see some succes in Slovak circles was the
nationalistic party.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:04.650
By the late 19th and early 20th century it
had a newspaper based from Martin called Národnie

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.110
noviny which was edited by Vajanský.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:11.770
This party as its name suggests was very much
nationalistic with some members bordering

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:13.950
on what we would today call fascism.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:18.090
Its agenda early on centered around the full
succession from the Empire and the creation

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.710
of independent Slovakia.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:25.520
On top of that, the party was known for its
Russophilia, anti-westernism, antisemitism

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:26.680
and agrarianism.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:31.760
After seeing no political success and very
strong suppression by the Hungarians the nationalistc

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:34.879
party became less radical going in to the
20th century.

00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:39.909
Abandoning the idea of full succession of
Slovakia and campaigning for universal suffrage

00:03:39.909 --> 00:03:42.660
and equal rights for Slovaks within the Empire.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:47.330
However anti westernism, anti semitism and
Russophilia still remained strong with the

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.800
more right leaning members of the party.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.161
Also the idea of a Czechoslovakian state was
very much a moot point with in the nationalistic

00:03:54.161 --> 00:03:56.190
circles not gaining any traction.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:04:00.830
And it is this political state that disgruntled
young Slovaks found themselves around the

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.209
turn of the century.

00:04:02.209 --> 00:04:06.470
With the only prominent political party being
very conservative and the Czechs pretty much

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:11.500
minding their own business giving the Slovaks
a thumbs up of encouragement across the Morava.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:16.250
But, this is all just one side of the story
and it is time to turn to the other side,

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:22.309
which largely revolves around one man, known
today as taticek Masaryk.

00:04:22.309 --> 00:04:28.259
Tomas Masaryk was born in a small town of
Hodonin right on the border between Czechia

00:04:28.259 --> 00:04:33.370
and Slovakia, when he was 6 his family moved
to a neighboring town of Cejkovice.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:37.520
His father was a Slovak farmer and his mother
a Germanized Moravian.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:42.479
Masaryk grew up speaking a zahoracky dialect
of Slovak but at an early age also learned

00:04:42.479 --> 00:04:44.219
German and Czech from his mother.

00:04:44.219 --> 00:04:49.199
He wasn’t particularly fond of manual labor
jobs preferring academia above all, for example

00:04:49.199 --> 00:04:53.889
as a teenager he taught himself Latin and
Ancient Greek just so he could read the original

00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:55.199
classical texts.

00:04:55.199 --> 00:04:59.969
He was also at the top of his class at a gymnazium
in Brno and later Vienna, while there he also

00:04:59.969 --> 00:05:04.990
learned French, Russian, Polish and English,
and earned a bit of money by translating documents

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:07.460
from those languages to German or Czech.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:12.130
Interestingly, while he was at gymnazium,
when he turned 16 he “joined a number of

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:16.659
young hotheads, who sallied forth to fight
for their country” in the Austro Prussian

00:05:16.659 --> 00:05:19.879
War also known in Germany as the Unification
War.

00:05:19.879 --> 00:05:24.879
He got injured during the war and recovered
in Bratislava before finishing up his gymnazium,

00:05:24.879 --> 00:05:29.020
after which he continued pursuing his passion
for academia enrolling at the University of

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:33.500
Vienna from which he got his eventual doctorate
in 1876.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:37.789
During this entire time Masaryk wasn’t involved
much in politics and even though he himself

00:05:37.789 --> 00:05:42.300
admitted to be a sympathiser for Czech and
Slovak autonomy, outside of joining a small

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:46.949
Slovak and Czech student unions in Vienna
he never actively did anything.

00:05:46.949 --> 00:05:53.009
Instead, he was fully immersed in his studies
of philosophy, history, psychology, etc.

00:05:53.009 --> 00:05:59.159
But that all changed in 1881/2 when he got
a post as a philosophy professor at Charles

00:05:59.159 --> 00:06:00.159
University.

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:03.999
It was in Prague that he was very much thrown
on to the Czech political stage through the

00:06:03.999 --> 00:06:09.050
academic connections he made there, all of
whom were already involved in politics.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:13.929
His early political life and ascendance is
quite complicated but the main event that

00:06:13.929 --> 00:06:16.650
can be pointed to is the Hilsner Case.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:21.979
The Hilsner Case was a series of trials against
a jewish peddler, for commiting a ritual murder

00:06:21.979 --> 00:06:24.120
of a young Czech girl.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:29.479
The evidence against him was laughable and
only situated on the unlikeability of his

00:06:29.479 --> 00:06:32.080
character and the fact that he was jewish.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.039
However most of the Czech politics at the
time involved anti semitism and much of the

00:06:36.039 --> 00:06:38.990
public wanted to see someone face some repercussions.

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:42.509
Masaryk however, even though stating he wasn’t
very fond of Hilsner.

00:06:42.509 --> 00:06:47.160
Decided to seemingly go against almost all
politicians and the public opinion, because

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:52.619
in his eyes this “monstrous non-legality”
could not stand in a just nation.

00:06:52.619 --> 00:06:57.809
With Masaryk’s help Hilsner was still convicted
but instead of being executed was given life

00:06:57.809 --> 00:06:59.149
imprisonment.

00:06:59.149 --> 00:07:03.870
During this nation wide incident Masaryk was
shown to the entire population as a honorous

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.729
man and fighter for justice.

00:07:05.729 --> 00:07:10.990
His idea of an “unpleasant truth is preferable
to a beneficial lie” became one of his core

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:16.289
political beliefs and he went on to find a
new Political Czech party called the Realists

00:07:16.289 --> 00:07:17.360
in 1900.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:22.009
This party was meant to replace the current
Young Czech Party that Masaryk viewed as pandering

00:07:22.009 --> 00:07:26.539
to the Empire just as well as to the Czech
people, resulting in nothing being done.

00:07:26.539 --> 00:07:31.069
The Realist party was very liberal for it’s
time, equating for full equality of women

00:07:31.069 --> 00:07:35.240
in the workplace, universal suffrage, freedom
of speech, etc.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:39.560
Also unlike the Czech parties up until now,
it actively worked with other Slavic parties

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.360
in Austria-Hungary, including Croats, Serbs,
Slovaks, etc.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:48.599
At the same time, Masaryk also helped coordinate
a small number of Slovak intellectuals studying

00:07:48.599 --> 00:07:53.639
in Czechia, to find a new political movement
against the conesrvative Slovak Nationalists.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:58.499
These people founded the newspaper ‘Hlas’
that focused around social democratic ideas

00:07:58.499 --> 00:08:02.139
and became a prominent counter to the Nationalistic
party.

00:08:02.139 --> 00:08:06.879
As the great war was drawing nigh almost none
of the major Czech or Slovak politicians,

00:08:06.879 --> 00:08:12.789
including Masaryk, propagated, at least officially,
any idea of succession from the Empire.

00:08:12.789 --> 00:08:17.709
Instead they all supported the proposed federalist
state of Austria-Hungary which was also supported

00:08:17.709 --> 00:08:19.619
by Archduke Franz Ferdinand.

00:08:19.619 --> 00:08:24.219
It also has to be noted that outside of a
small minority, like the group Českoslovanská

00:08:24.219 --> 00:08:30.080
jednota, the idea of a Czechslovak state was
never proposed on any major political level.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:34.409
Even Masaryk, though his actions and rhetoric
in the early 19th century where very much

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:40.039
so heading towards a unified Czechoslovakia,
never actually publicly stated he wanted a

00:08:40.039 --> 00:08:42.729
Czechoslovak union until 1907.

00:08:42.729 --> 00:08:46.730
Most scholars today believe it was his plan
all along to unify the Czechs and Slovaks,

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:51.600
a people who he called ‘co-nationals’,
he just wanted to sture up more political

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:55.529
support for such a move before declaring it
officially.

00:08:55.529 --> 00:08:58.949
And reading his lecture notes I think this
becomes very clear.

00:08:58.949 --> 00:09:03.540
Nonetheless, whatever the political agenda
and views both sides had, when it became clear

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:08.680
that the Great War was inevitable, the Czechs
and Slovaks started to view a mutual cooperation

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:12.360
as the best chance towards an independent
and strong country.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:17.120
And just like that, Masaryk who was working
towards a unified Czechoslovak state for decades

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:21.839
now, became the center point of the Czechoslovak
independence movement during the war.

00:09:21.839 --> 00:09:26.399
At the start of the war Masaryk viewed the
German and Austrian mobilization and he had

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:27.399
this to say.

00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:32.600
“I could not help feeling impressed by the
purposeful [German] discipline and the preparedness

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:34.510
to the last button.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:39.820
Throughout the mobilization I did not see
a single drunken German, whereas the contingents

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:46.699
of Austrian recruits on their way home to
join [the war,] were, for the most part, helplessly

00:09:46.699 --> 00:09:48.709
intoxicated.”

00:09:48.709 --> 00:09:51.800
No real point from this quote, I just thought
it was funny.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:56.399
However two quotes do summarize Masaryk’s
life for the next 4 years quite well.

00:09:56.399 --> 00:10:00.500
Saenger a man who meat Masaryk at the beginning
of the war said this.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:04.750
“The impression which Masaryk produced on
me was extraordinary.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:10.440
He was entirely taken up with one single idea
… this man, who was an Austrian against

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:16.420
his will, was engrossed by the question whether
the historical moment had come when the Empire

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:20.230
was to be split up into its national ingredients.”

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:26.660
During this time Masaryk also meat with Professor
Seton-Watson with whom he created the Memorandum

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:28.000
for Central Europe.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.380
Watson later said this about that.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:35.939
“The programme which Masaryk placed before
me at that secret meeting in a hotel Rotterdam

00:10:35.939 --> 00:10:42.930
in October, 1914, was fulfilled almost to
the letter in October, 1918.”

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:46.800
So Masaryk had a plan, and he had the will
to execute it.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:51.259
Therefore the next 4 years Masaryk took the
initiative, almost single handedly getting

00:10:51.259 --> 00:10:56.490
diplomatic support for the creation of Czechoslovakia
across the world.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:58.291
He traveled to
Rotterdam 1914

00:10:58.291 --> 00:10:59.750
Geneva 1915
Paris 1915-1917

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:00.750
London 1915-1917
Petrograd

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:01.750
Moscow
Kiev

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.060
Vladivostok
Tokyo

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:04.439
Chicago
Washington

00:11:04.439 --> 00:11:05.509
New York
London

00:11:05.509 --> 00:11:08.810
Paris
And in 1918 Prague

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:13.470
Masaryk was the one to organize the Czechoslovak
legion in Russia and later he was the one

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:16.759
to negotiate safe passage of this legion across
Russia.

00:11:16.759 --> 00:11:20.890
He also had time to be one of the founders
of the UCL School of Slavonic and East European

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:24.649
Studies in London and many other things we
don’t have time to talk about.

00:11:24.649 --> 00:11:28.629
However it wasn’t all smooth sailing for
gaining diplomatic support for the creation

00:11:28.629 --> 00:11:29.970
of Czechoslovakia.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:33.899
The most prominent opposition coming from
the British, who didn’t want to break up

00:11:33.899 --> 00:11:37.370
the Austro-Hungarian Empire, especially not
at the start of the War.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:41.779
America on the other hand proved to be the
most enthusiastic allie of Masaryk and his

00:11:41.779 --> 00:11:42.949
cause.

00:11:42.949 --> 00:11:49.110
When he arrived to Chicago, he was joyfully
greeted by 150 thousands people, most of which

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:51.230
where of Czechoslovak Origin.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:55.970
Eventually thanks to Masaryk unrelentless
diplomatic work, a new nation was founded,

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:58.690
a Czechoslovak nation.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:13.360
Unsurprisingly, Masaryk

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:18.510
was elected as the first president of Czechoslovakia,
and a new chapter not just in Masaryk’s

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:22.639
life but in Czechoslovak history began.

00:12:22.639 --> 00:12:29.670
A chapter that until 1938, had a lot of its
own problems, but that’s a story for another

00:12:29.670 --> 00:12:31.750
time.

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:36.180
This video is part of a greater Project Homecoming,
where for the holidays a bunch of History

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:40.870
YouTubers are talking about the history of
where they live or where they’re from.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:44.670
Since I am from Slovakia, I talked about the
formation of Czechoslovakia.

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:48.480
If you want to see other history youtubers’
videos, click the link to the playlist on

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.399
the screen or in the description.

00:12:50.399 --> 00:12:52.550
My name is M. Laser and see you next time.

